# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Enchanting --out` from tools/lib/professions/routes/enchanting.json and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/enchanting
title Enchanting 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Enchanting puts lasting magic on gear and makes oils and wands. Its materials come from breaking
# green items with Disenchant, which Enchanting teaches, or from the Auction House; no gathering
# profession is needed. Tailoring is a good partner: its green cloth items break into dust.
#
# Disenchanting gives skill too: a point for nearly every item up to 20, fewer after that, none from
# 60. Every enchant goes onto an item, worn or in the bags, and one item takes them all.
#
# Ranks: Apprentice at any level from any Enchanting trainer (the first trainer teaches recipes only
# up to 70); Journeyman from level 10 at the city trainers; Expert from level 20 at Kitta Firewind
# or Hgarth; Artisan from level 35 at Annora, inside Uldaman, the only trainer of that rank.
#
# The route (crafts are about what it takes; yellow and green recipes can take a few more):
# Apprentice (1-70), from level 1:
#    1-2   1 Runed Copper Rod: 1 Copper Rod, 1 Mote of Magic
#    2-20  disenchant green items (a point for nearly each)
#    2-20  18 Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina: 18 Mote of Magic
#   20-70  50 Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina: 50 Strange Dust
# Journeyman (70-150), from level 10:
#   70-85  21 Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina: 21 Strange Dust
#   85-100 15 Enchant Bracer - Minor Stamina: 30 Strange Dust
#  100-109 9 Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection: 18 Strange Dust
#  109-110 1 Runed Silver Rod: 1 Shadowgem, 1 Silver Rod, 4 Lesser Magic Essence, 3 Strange Dust
#  110-130 29 Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection: 58 Strange Dust
#  130-150 20 Enchant Boots - Minor Stamina: 80 Strange Dust
# Expert (150-225), from level 20:
#  150-151 1 Runed Golden Rod: 1 Iridescent Pearl, 1 Greater Astral Essence, 1 Soul Dust, 1 Golden Rod
#  151-165 16 Minor Mana Oil: 16 Leaded Vial, 16 Soul Dust, 32 Maple Seed
#  165-200 44 Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility: 44 Soul Dust
#  200-201 1 Runed Truesilver Rod: 1 Black Pearl, 1 Greater Mystic Essence, 1 Vision Dust, 1 Truesilver Rod
#  201-220 25 Lesser Wizard Oil: 25 Leaded Vial, 25 Vision Dust, 50 Stranglethorn Seed
#  220-225 5 Enchant Cloak - Greater Defense: 5 Vision Dust
# Artisan (225-300), from level 35:
#  225-250 34 Enchant Gloves - Agility: 34 Vision Dust
#  250-270 26 Lesser Mana Oil: 26 Purple Lotus, 26 Crystal Vial, 26 Dream Dust
#  270-275 5 Enchant Shield - Greater Stamina: 30 Dream Dust
#  275-295 26 Wizard Oil: 52 Firebloom, 26 Crystal Vial, 78 Illusion Dust
#  295-299 8 Enchant Shield - Greater Stamina: 48 Dream Dust
#  299-300 1 Runed Arcanite Rod: 1 Golden Pearl, 4 Small Brilliant Shard, 2 Large Brilliant Shard, 4 Greater Eternal Essence, 10 Illusion Dust, 1 Arcanite Rod

section Enchanting 1-2

step Learn Enchanting
  tip No character level needed.
  train Enchanting Apprentice

step Buy 1 Copper Rod
  tip For 1 Runed Copper Rod.
  buy 6217 x1 nearest

step Buy 19 Motes of Magic
  tip For 1 Runed Copper Rod and 18 Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina.
  buy 247786 x19 nearest

step Craft 1 Runed Copper Rod
  tip It takes Enchanting to about 2. A tool: it stays in your bags, and every enchant needs it.
  craft 7421 x1

section Enchanting 2-20

step Disenchant your green items until 20
  tip Disenchant is in the Enchanting window, not the spellbook. Nearly every item gives a point below 20.
  skill Enchanting 20 either
  task "No green items left to break" either

step Craft 18 Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina until 20
  tip Only if disenchanting didn't get you to 20. Any bracer you wear or carry takes them all, one over the last.
  craft 7418 until 20

